00:04:55.604 --> 00:04:59.161
So let's see from Facebook, Snahat Nath,

00:04:59.161 --> 00:05:01.774
"Do you think standardized
testing will always be here

00:05:01.774 --> 00:05:04.534
or do you think something
else will replace them?"

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:08.004
Well, you know, sometimes,
you know, standardized testing

00:05:08.004 --> 00:05:10.574
a lot of people, you know, say, oh

00:05:10.574 --> 00:05:13.664
well, that, that gives, you
know, it creates stress and all

00:05:13.664 --> 00:05:14.504
of these types of things.

00:05:14.504 --> 00:05:19.204
But I always remind folks
that, you know, the opposite

00:05:19.204 --> 00:05:21.964
of standardized testing is
non-standardized testing

00:05:21.964 --> 00:05:23.624
or not testing at all.

00:05:23.624 --> 00:05:25.394
And if you're not measuring something

00:05:25.394 --> 00:05:27.564
it's very hard to know
whether, you know it

00:05:27.564 --> 00:05:30.534
or whether you're growing
or how well you know it.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:31.367
And if it's done

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:34.884
in a non-standardized way,
well, that's not much better

00:05:34.884 --> 00:05:38.164
because how do you understand
where you are compared

00:05:38.164 --> 00:05:41.134
to where you need to be
in a standardized way?

00:05:41.134 --> 00:05:43.636
So I would say that, you
know, generally speaking

00:05:43.636 --> 00:05:47.324
in the world, you do need
standardized measurement

00:05:47.324 --> 00:05:50.254
and standardized testing is that is a form

00:05:50.254 --> 00:05:53.744
of standardized measurement
that we use in academics.

00:05:53.744 --> 00:05:54.914
Now I do think

00:05:54.914 --> 00:05:57.544
over time, standardized
testing is going to be expanded

00:05:57.544 --> 00:05:58.544
or it's going to evolve.

00:05:58.544 --> 00:05:59.377
I think the types

00:05:59.377 --> 00:06:01.064
of standardized testing
that we're familiar

00:06:01.064 --> 00:06:03.864
with, I think you'll always
have standardized tests.

00:06:03.864 --> 00:06:06.744
That'll be, you know, how well
can you factor a polynomial?

00:06:06.744 --> 00:06:10.374
How well, how strong is
your reading comprehension?

00:06:10.374 --> 00:06:11.774
But I think then those
are going to be expanded

00:06:11.774 --> 00:06:15.564
with new forms of standardized
assessment where, you know

00:06:15.564 --> 00:06:19.634
maybe there's some type of how
well can you teach a subject?

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:20.994
How well can you

00:06:23.204 --> 00:06:25.754
you know, compose a poem
or something like this

00:06:25.754 --> 00:06:27.904
and that, you know,
having interesting ways

00:06:27.904 --> 00:06:29.944
for maybe the community
to help evaluate you

00:06:29.944 --> 00:06:31.954
in a standardized way.

00:06:31.954 --> 00:06:35.544
So I don't think the notion
of standardized measurement

00:06:35.544 --> 00:06:37.474
or standardized tests are going away

00:06:37.474 --> 00:06:39.034
nor should they go away.

00:06:39.034 --> 00:06:42.154
But I think over time they will
evolve and we'll have a kind

00:06:42.154 --> 00:06:43.304
of a broader aperture

00:06:43.304 --> 00:06:45.304
of what and how they can measure things.

00:06:46.474 --> 00:06:48.464
So let's see,

00:06:48.464 --> 00:06:51.974
from Facebook Rom says,
"Why do you use your name?

00:06:51.974 --> 00:06:55.504
Why don't you use your name
as Salmaan instead of Sal?"

00:06:55.504 --> 00:06:58.114
So Salmaan is my, my full first name.

00:06:58.114 --> 00:07:00.184
My full name is Salmaan Khan.

00:07:00.184 --> 00:07:01.384
So the reason why I go

00:07:01.384 --> 00:07:04.664
by Sal, you know, it's really
what my mother has called me

00:07:04.664 --> 00:07:05.497
from the beginning.

00:07:05.497 --> 00:07:06.724
So this, you know

00:07:06.724 --> 00:07:09.144
a lot of times folks, especially

00:07:09.144 --> 00:07:11.774
folks who have a name that is not

00:07:11.774 --> 00:07:13.374
familiar to folks where they live

00:07:13.374 --> 00:07:14.724
they'll sometimes shorten their names.

00:07:14.724 --> 00:07:15.557
And you know

00:07:15.557 --> 00:07:17.554
definitely a lot of folks
in my family have done that.

00:07:17.554 --> 00:07:19.604
My mother's name is Masuda.

00:07:19.604 --> 00:07:23.514
And for convenience purposes,
I was probably around 12

00:07:23.514 --> 00:07:25.312
or 13 years when she decided to tell

00:07:25.312 --> 00:07:26.744
people who are not familiar

00:07:26.744 --> 00:07:29.469
with the name of Sue though,
that her name was Sue.

00:07:29.469 --> 00:07:32.554
You know, I have an Uncle Azad.

00:07:32.554 --> 00:07:33.894
He goes by Zach.

00:07:33.894 --> 00:07:35.564
I have an Uncle Mucbul.

00:07:35.564 --> 00:07:37.364
He goes by Mac.

00:07:37.364 --> 00:07:39.544
I have an Uncle Khalid who actually goes

00:07:39.544 --> 00:07:42.424
by Jason, which is completely unrelated.

00:07:42.424 --> 00:07:43.624
He was a, he worked

00:07:43.624 --> 00:07:46.614
on a ship for a while and he
was always fascinated by Jason

00:07:46.614 --> 00:07:47.504
the famous sailor.

00:07:47.504 --> 00:07:50.224
I have an Uncle Arshot who goes

00:07:50.224 --> 00:07:52.244
by Daniel, once again,

00:07:52.244 --> 00:07:54.782
not an obvious shortening of the name.

00:07:54.782 --> 00:07:57.496
He, he liked that song, you know.

00:07:57.496 --> 00:07:59.904
♪ Daniel is traveling tonight on a plane ♪

00:07:59.904 --> 00:08:02.474
Anyway, long story short,
that's not the cause

00:08:02.474 --> 00:08:05.594
of my name going from Salmaan to to Sal.

00:08:05.594 --> 00:08:08.414
It really is that my mom,
I think just found it

00:08:08.414 --> 00:08:11.374
convenient to call me Sal
when I was growing up.

00:08:11.374 --> 00:08:14.353
And then it did just happen
to kind of stick in my head

00:08:14.353 --> 00:08:18.853
but I respond to either Sal or Salmaan,

00:08:18.853 --> 00:08:20.587
whatever works for folks.

00:08:22.254 --> 00:08:25.434
Let's see other questions here

00:08:26.914 --> 00:08:29.497
from, see, I answered that one.

00:08:30.504 --> 00:08:31.444
So from YouTube

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:32.981
Joshua Katavil said,

00:08:32.981 --> 00:08:34.464
"How do you think
artificial intelligence will

00:08:34.464 --> 00:08:38.814
either help or damage the
current world of technology?"

00:08:38.814 --> 00:08:39.854
That's a big question.

00:08:39.854 --> 00:08:43.464
I don't claim to be the
world's leading expert

00:08:43.464 --> 00:08:44.614
on artificial intelligence.

00:08:44.614 --> 00:08:48.447
But I do like to traffic
in futurist ideas.

00:08:50.934 --> 00:08:52.114
I, first of all

00:08:52.114 --> 00:08:53.554
I think the genie's out of the box.

00:08:53.554 --> 00:08:56.054
Artificial intelligence is
going to be increasingly used.

00:08:56.054 --> 00:08:56.944
I think one of the hard things

00:08:56.944 --> 00:08:59.867
about artificial
intelligence is it can create

00:08:59.867 --> 00:09:03.094
you know, positive optimizations
for a lot of things

00:09:03.094 --> 00:09:06.114
but sometimes you don't know
why it's choosing one thing

00:09:06.114 --> 00:09:07.614
or another.

00:09:07.614 --> 00:09:10.544
And so I think artificial
intelligence can have many

00:09:10.544 --> 00:09:12.984
many very, very positive uses.

00:09:12.984 --> 00:09:15.114
You know, a lot of mundane human tasks

00:09:15.114 --> 00:09:16.524
will not have to be done

00:09:16.524 --> 00:09:19.014
in a mundane way by human beings.

00:09:19.014 --> 00:09:20.944
You'll have, I could imagine artificial

00:09:20.944 --> 00:09:25.644
intelligence is that can
help improve your motivation,

00:09:25.644 --> 00:09:27.284
that can help you learn.

00:09:27.284 --> 00:09:28.384
Hopefully one day Khan Academy

00:09:28.384 --> 00:09:30.014
can incorporate things like that

00:09:30.014 --> 00:09:32.814
that can improve your
relationship with someone else.

00:09:32.814 --> 00:09:34.932
You know, it asks the right questions so

00:09:34.932 --> 00:09:38.254
that it builds bonds between
you and another human being.

00:09:38.254 --> 00:09:39.674
You know, yesterday we talked a lot

00:09:39.674 --> 00:09:41.004
with the former surgeon general

00:09:41.004 --> 00:09:42.824
about kind of a loneliness epidemic.

00:09:42.824 --> 00:09:46.224
And, you know, it seems
a little dystopian if

00:09:46.224 --> 00:09:47.924
your loneliness is partly addressed

00:09:47.924 --> 00:09:49.077
with an artificial intelligence

00:09:49.077 --> 00:09:52.024
but there is, you know,
maybe something powerful

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:54.744
about, you know, sometimes
being able to confide

00:09:54.744 --> 00:09:58.085
in something that, you
know, isn't going to,

00:09:58.085 --> 00:10:00.884
where your secrets are safe.

00:10:00.884 --> 00:10:02.804
So I dunno, there, there could
be some positive use cases

00:10:02.804 --> 00:10:03.684
but then there could be a lot of

00:10:03.684 --> 00:10:05.164
weird use cases too.

00:10:05.164 --> 00:10:07.604
I mean, that last one I
gave where, where people's

00:10:07.604 --> 00:10:12.254
best friends ended up becoming
not a real human being

00:10:12.254 --> 00:10:14.226
or artificial intelligence is

00:10:14.226 --> 00:10:16.494
you know, there's several examples

00:10:16.494 --> 00:10:19.074
of them developing their own
biases based on the data that

00:10:19.074 --> 00:10:21.354
I mean, in fact, a lot of machine learning

00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:25.504
is all about kind of
forming a bias, but some

00:10:25.504 --> 00:10:28.074
of those biases can be very,
very unhealthy and you don't

00:10:28.074 --> 00:10:31.144
and it might be expressing
in very subtle ways.

00:10:31.144 --> 00:10:32.754
So, yeah, I think it's going to be very

00:10:32.754 --> 00:10:34.074
it's going to be a brave new world.

00:10:34.074 --> 00:10:37.218
The next 10 or 20 years is,
you know, we really grapple

00:10:37.218 --> 00:10:39.924
with how artificial intelligence is used

00:10:39.924 --> 00:10:44.064
or not, but it's gonna,
it's gonna be interesting.

